# Node identity and key material — NEVER commit this.
#
# `identity/` holds this node's federation keys: sealed classical Ed25519 seed
# blobs (`<alias>.ed25519.seed.blob`), their 32-byte master keys
# (`<alias>.master.key`), the TPM seal, and the bare ML-DSA-65 PQC seed. Every
# boot of a checkout mints another set, so the directory accumulates silently —
# 124 of these files were tracked before this rule existed, and 122 reached
# main.
#
# A committed private key is compromised the moment it is pushed, and it stays
# in history after the file is deleted. The matching rule already exists in
# .dockerignore for the same reason (key material must not ride inside an image
# layer either); git needed its own.
#
# A node MINTS its identity — persist's create_identity_if_missing does it at
# boot. There is no case where a checkout should carry one.
identity/
keys/

# First-run node state produced by running a node from the checkout.
ceg/
claim_pin

# iOS native substrate payload — FETCHED, not tracked.
#
# tools/update_substrate_libs.py downloads the ciris-server wheel and stages
# `_native.abi3.so` here (75 MB) on the way to building Resources.zip. Its
# siblings (aiohttp, cryptography, pydantic_core) are tracked for historical
# reasons; this one is not, because a build artifact a script fetches on demand
# does not belong in git — the same rule that keeps pre-built binaries out (see
# tools/update_ciris_verify.py for the canonical fetch-on-install pattern).
#
# Run the updater to populate it:
#   python -m tools.update_substrate_libs --platform ios --lib server <version>
client/iosApp/app_packages_native/ciris_server/
